      "obligation": "refuter:8:1",
      "id": "lem-sr-four-momentum-in-inertial-frame",
      "location": "Statement (c), first displayed boost formulas",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The statement defines “β=(v/c)s” with s∈R³, then writes P'^0=γ_v(P^0−β s·p) and p'_parallel=γ_v(p_parallel−β P^0 s). Thus β is a three-vector: the first formula subtracts a vector from the scalar P^0, and the second uses an undefined product of two spatial vectors. The opened dependency def-lorentz-boost defines a vector parameter and gives x'^0=γ(x^0−boldsymbolβ·x_vec), not the displayed expression. Proof step 1.3 correctly derives P'^0=γ_v(P^0−(v/c)p_parallel) and p'=p_perp+γ_v(p_parallel−(v/c)P^0)s; those scalar formulas do not license the ill-formed statement.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "9c45618c5d771e67250e2c083d88efe0397cae1d9a5c586ead141008811cd6bc"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:8:2",
      "id": "lem-sr-center-of-momentum-frame",
      "location": "title",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The title asserts “Existence and uniqueness of the center-of-momentum frame of a future timelike four-momentum”. The opened definition def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass (c) defines a frame as the tuple (o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3). For Q=Mc e_0, both (o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3) and (o+e_1;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3) are distinct center-of-momentum frames, since the projection condition is independent of the origin. Spatial rotations give further distinct frames. Statement (b) and proof step 2.2 correctly establish uniqueness only of the time vector, with arbitrary origin and spatial-rotation freedom; the unqualified uniqueness asserted by the title is stronger.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "9f9d0b67cc67ee220be29639a18f7203a8f98b905ab7ea74ada2f7f98276b947"
    }
